6726: \subsection{Subordinate support-boundary ledger}
6727: 
6728: The material in this subsection is deliberately bounded to this package: it only
6729: records when the finite review-bundle rows cited above remain local/path-verified
6730: and what finite coordinate would upgrade them to external support.  A general
6731: calculus of support-surface replacement, archive locators, and digest-preserving
6732: mirrors is a split-candidate infrastructure note rather than an additional theorem
6733: package for the present CICM presentation route.
6734: 
6735: \begin{table}
6736: \caption{Finite archive-equivalence criterion for replacing the review bundle.}
6737: \label{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}
6738: \scriptsize
6739: \begin{tabularx}{\linewidth}{p{0.25\linewidth}X p{0.25\linewidth}}
6740: \toprule
6741: Criterion & Required data in the archive replacement & Failure effect \\
6742: \midrule
6743: Manifest identity & a root record byte-identical to \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}, except for an added archive URL or DOI field that is not used by the verifier & replacement rejected \\
6744: Bundle version & the identity tuple \path{(supplemental_review_bundle, 2026-06-01, 3fb3d6a0641767388a401883062aa522ea0b397b)} from the manifest fields \path{bundle_kind}, \path{created}, and \path{public_interface.public_source_commit} & replacement rejected \\
6745: Finite file list & exactly the regular files named by the manifest, submission-interface map, source-snapshot record, case-snapshot rows, verifier-script fields, and verifier-log fields; generated cache files such as \path{__pycache__/} are excluded & replacement rejected \\
6746: Content hashes & a SHA-256 digest for each file in that finite file list, equal to the digest of the corresponding file in the submitted \path{review_bundle/} at final packaging time & replacement rejected \\
6747: Path semantics & every path in the archive preserves the same relative name below \path{review_bundle/} and no certificate row is retargeted to a different file & replacement rejected \\
6748: \bottomrule
6749: \end{tabularx}
6750: \end{table}
6751: 
6752: \begin{auditrecord}[Review-bundle archive-equivalence criterion]
6753: \label{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}
6754: An archival replacement for \path{review_bundle/} is accepted by this manuscript
6755: only if it satisfies all rows of
6756: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Equivalently, it must have
6757: the same manifest identity, the same bundle-version tuple, the same finite
6758: certificate file list, the same SHA-256 content digests at final packaging time,
6759: and the same relative path semantics as the submitted \path{review_bundle/}.
6760: If no such hash-and-manifest archive is supplied, the only recorded support
6761: surface is the local \path{review_bundle/} directory; this audit record does not
6762: assert that the directory has been uploaded.
6763: \medskip
6764: \noindent\emph{Verification.} The manifest identity criterion fixes the root record that all bundle-dependent
6765: claims cite: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}.  Allowing only an
6766: additional archive locator field prevents the archive from silently changing the
6767: certificate schema, pass-record ledger, submission-interface map,
6768: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts, verifier logs, pinned-source
6769: snapshot, case-evidence rows, or submission-artifact declaration.  The bundle
6770: version is finite because the current manifest carries the three displayed
6771: fields \path{bundle_kind}, \path{created}, and
6772: \path{public_interface.public_source_commit}; equality of the tuple rules out
6773: substituting a different support bundle or a different pinned source commit.
6774: 
6775: The finite file-list criterion is obtained by following only the manifest and
6776: the machine-readable interface records already used in the proofs: certificate
6777: schema, current pass records, primary-claim inventory, submission-interface map,
6778: verifier scripts and logs, source snapshot, and the case snapshots named in the
6779: case-evidence rows.  This traversal is finite because each record is a finite
6780: JSON or manuscript table row and because generated interpreter caches are not
6781: certificate surfaces.  The content-hash criterion then gives a byte-level test
6782: for every file on that finite list.  If a file is omitted, added as a replacement
6783: for a named certificate surface, or changed bytewise, either the file-list row or
6784: the SHA-256 row fails.  The path-semantics row prevents a hash-correct file from
6785: being moved under a new relative name that would make manuscript paths point to a
6786: different object.
6787: 
6788: When all five rows pass, every path used by a bundle-dependent theorem,
6789: proposition, table row, verifier record, or manifest row denotes the same bytes
6790: under the same relative name and under the same root manifest identity as in the
6791: submitted \path{review_bundle/}.  Thus the archive is equivalent for exactly the
6792: finite certificate checks made in this paper.  When any row fails, a reviewer has
6793: a finite bad subrecord: the changed manifest identity, changed version tuple,
6794: file-list discrepancy, hash mismatch, or path-retargeting witness.  In that case
6795: the archive is not accepted, and the current support surface remains the local
6796: \path{review_bundle/} directory unless a later upload or byte-equality coordinate
6797: is added.
6798: \end{auditrecord}
6799: 
