6888: \begin{theorem}[Finite-record support invariant: exact-inclusion support surface]
6889: \label{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}
6890: For the current package the selected support branch is exact supplemental
6891: inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, but this branch remains conditional until an
6892: external upload-or-archive instantiation record exists.  If the completed
6893: submission contains that directory, together with \path{theorem_inventory.json}
6894: and \path{theorem_inventory.md}, and those three support surfaces match the
6895: post-inventory digest rows listed in
6896: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}, then every bundle-backed claim in
6897: this supplement has a submitted finite support surface at its stated
6898: path-verified evidence level.  If the exact directory is not submitted, then the
6899: same support conclusion holds only after replacing it by an archive satisfying
6900: the five tests of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}; no venue upload receipt or public DOI is claimed for the present package, and the public automath branch/path coordinate is only a candidate archive-equivalent locator unless a finite byte-equality record supplies matching digest rows.
6901: \end{theorem}
6902: 
6903: \begin{proof}
6904: The exact-inclusion hypothesis supplies the two root inventory files, the
6905: directory named in every bundle-local path, and the final digest manifest named
6906: in Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}.  By that
6907: proposition, the manifest traverses the finite certificate surfaces used by the
6908: supplement: the theorem-obligation inventories, the bundle manifest, schema,
6909: current pass-record ledger, source-interface map, primary-claim inventory,
6910: verifier scripts, verifier logs, source snapshot, and case snapshots.  Matching
6911: the listed SHA-256 digests fixes the bytes of each of those certificate files at
6912: final packaging time, while preserving the relative path names by which the
6913: manuscript refers to them.  Thus every bundle-backed claim has the submitted
6914: finite evidence surface asserted for it, and the evidence level remains
6915: path-verified because the argument checks file presence and digest identity
6916: rather than rerunning Lean, daemons, or external artifacts.
6917: 
6918: If the exact directory is absent, the proof of
6919: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} shows that the only
6920: finite replacement accepted by this paper is an archive with the same manifest
6921: identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list, per-file SHA-256
6922: digests, and relative path semantics.  Those are exactly the five tests in
6923: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Without such an archive, at
6924: least one bundle-local path or digest row has no submitted representative, so the
6925: corresponding bundle-backed claim lacks its evidence surface.  The statement that
6926: no public DOI or venue-upload receipt is claimed is the support-mode boundary in
6927: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}; the public branch/path
6928: coordinate is an archive-equivalent locator only under the same byte, digest, and
6929: path-semantics tests.
6930: \end{proof}
6931: 
6932: \begin{theorem}[Finite-record support invariant: public branch locator criterion]
6933: \label{thm:public-branch-archive-equivalent-realization}
6934: Let $L$ be the public automath branch/path coordinate recorded in
6935: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json} and in the support-boundary
6936: text of this supplement.  If $L$ contains
6937: \path{theorem_inventory.json}, \path{theorem_inventory.md}, and the regular files
6938: under \path{review_bundle/} with the same relative paths and the SHA--256 rows
6939: printed in \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}, and if $L$ is pinned by
6940: commit or immutable release identifier, or else the branch head and
6941: byte-equality record are refreshed together at the final support state, then $L$ is an
6942: archive-equivalent support surface for every bundle-backed and theorem-inventory
6943: claim in this supplement.  If any named file is absent at $L$, has a different
6944: relative path, has a digest different from the final digest row, or lacks the
6945: required immutability or same-state branch-head record, then $L$ does
6946: not instantiate those claims, and the package falls back to exact supplemental
6947: inclusion or to the local/path-verified reading.  The present source package
6948: does not assert that the displayed public coordinate already satisfies these
6949: byte-equality tests; it asserts only this finite criterion and the corresponding
6950: conditional archive-equivalence branch.
6951: \end{theorem}
6952: 
6953: \begin{proof}
6954: The locator $L$ is finite for the purposes of this paper because the accepted
6955: support surface is not the whole repository: it is the displayed relative
6956: package path, the two theorem-inventory files, the finite regular-file list below
6957: \path{review_bundle/}, and the final digest table.  The bundle manifest and
6958: support-boundary text name the same repository, branch, and package path, so a
6959: reviewer can compare a candidate public surface against the finite table in
6960: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.
6961: 
6962: Assume first that all listed files are present at $L$ with the displayed relative
6963: paths and digests, and that $L$ is pinned by an immutable identifier or by a
6964: same-state branch-head byte-equality record.  Then every manuscript reference to a theorem-inventory or
6965: bundle-local certificate file denotes the same byte string at $L$ as in the exact
6966: support tuple, with no later branch movement hidden inside the locator.  The manifest identity, file-list, content-hash, and path-semantics
6967: requirements of Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} are
6968: therefore satisfied, while Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}
6969: proves that those same bytes are sufficient for the stated path-verified evidence
6970: level.  Thus $L$ realizes the archive-equivalent branch of
6971: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}.
6972: 
6973: Conversely, suppose a named file is missing, moved, digest-mismatched, or not tied
6974: to the same final support state by an immutable identifier or refreshed
6975: branch-head record.  Then at least one of the finite tests in
6976: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} fails: the file-list
6977: row fails for absence, the path-semantics row fails for a move, or the hash row
6978: fails for byte mismatch or mutable-state ambiguity.  The failed row is a finite bad subrecord, so
6979: Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form} rejects the archive-equivalent
6980: reading.  No DOI, venue-upload receipt, Lean rebuild, daemon execution, or
6981: artifact-validation fact follows from the locator comparison, so the only
6982: remaining readings are exact supplemental inclusion when supplied, or the local
6983: path-verified reading already classified above.
6984: 
6985: Finally, the current package contains no finite byte-equality record witnessing
6986: that the public coordinate has passed the displayed comparison at a pinned commit
6987: or refreshed branch head.  By
6988: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}, such a witness cannot
6989: be inferred from the local manifest, support-boundary text, or branch/path name
6990: alone.  Hence this theorem is an archive-equivalence criterion rather than a
6991: claim that an external archive has already been instantiated.
6992: \end{proof}
6993: 
6994: \begin{corollary}[Submission-time support instantiation test]
6995: \label{cor:submission-time-support-instantiation-test}
6996: For a completed presentation-only submission, the bundle-backed and
6997: venue/bibliography-backed claims in this package instantiate external support if
6998: and only if the submitted support surface contains one of the following finite
6999: normal forms:
7000: \begin{enumerate}
7001: \item exact inclusion of \path{theorem_inventory.json},
7002:   \path{theorem_inventory.md}, and \path{review_bundle/}, with
7003:   \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} regenerated after the inventory,
7004:   extractor, verifier, primary-claim-freshness, and venue/bibliography records
7005:   used by the submission are final;
7006: \item an archive-equivalent replacement carrying the same relative file list,
7007:   path semantics, manifest rows, SHA--256 digests, and upload-or-archive locator;
7008:   or
7009: \item a later replacement support surface with the same fields and a later
7010:   venue/bibliography verification record run immediately before submission.
7011: \end{enumerate}
7012: Without one of these finite records, the same claims remain only local or dated
7013: path-verified observations and do not certify external bundle availability,
7014: upload-time venue compliance, bibliography freshness, DOI availability, archive
7015: availability, Lean/BEDC rebuilds, or dynamic artifact validation.
7016: \end{corollary}
7017: 
7018: \begin{proof}
7019: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization} proves the exact
7020: inclusion branch: submitted byte identity for the selected support directory and
7021: its digest manifest gives the finite evidence surface for bundle-backed claims.
7022: The same theorem, through Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence},
7023: proves the archive branch, because the archive tests preserve the finite file
7024: list, relative paths, manifest identity, and per-file SHA--256 rows used by the
7025: bundle-local references.  The replacement branch is
7026: Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation} applied with a new
7027: commit--manifest certificate, together with the freshness condition of
7028: Proposition~\ref{audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion} for venue and bibliography
7029: claims.
7030: 
7031: It remains only to justify the ``only if'' direction.  By
7032: Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}, every accepted external support
7033: reading is either the selected directory, an archive-equivalent representative,
7034: or a deliberately promoted replacement state.  The post-inventory ordering is
7035: the fixed-point requirement in
7036: Theorem~\ref{thm:post-inventory-package-fixed-point}: if the digest precedes the
7037: inventory bytes or the post-inventory logs, at least one submitted digest row is
7038: not a digest of the byte string used by the claim.  Venue and bibliography pages
7039: are time-sensitive, so Proposition~\ref{audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion}
7040: allows a current compliance reading only on the checked rule state or after a
7041: later record with the same fields.  If none of the three displayed normal forms
7042: is present, Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} forbids
7043: inserting the missing locator, digest, freshness, or command fields by prose.
7044: The final sentence is exactly the non-escalation boundary established in
7045: Theorem~\ref{thm:submission-support-fixed-point-normal-form}.
7046: \end{proof}
7047: 
7048: \begin{theorem}[Finite-record support invariant: final support-surface closure]
7049: \label{thm:final-support-surface-closure}
7050: For the current package, using
7051: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention},
7052: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}, and
7053: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}, the bundle-backed
7054: claims in this supplement are admissible at the stated local/path-verified
7055: evidence level exactly when the local support surface contains the exact directory
7056: \path{review_bundle/} whose final packaging record is
7057: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  The local directory branch also
7058: requires that any post-generation change to a named bundle file be followed by
7059: refreshed SHA-256 rows in that final digest record and by rerunning the finite
7060: verifiers whose records cite the changed coordinate.  A replacement archive is not
7061: a current package branch; it would have to satisfy
7062: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} and provide a locator before a
7063: future package could select it.  If the exact directory is not present locally,
7064: the bundle-backed claims are not part of the accepted local support surface,
7065: although the short presentation artifact may still cite the pinned public
7066: \path{newmath} repository for the imported source spine.
7067: \end{theorem}
7068: 
7069: \begin{proof}
7070: Let $B$ denote the set of bundle-dependent claims in this supplement.  By the
7071: definition of \path{review_bundle/} in the problem statement and by the bundle
7072: rows of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, every claim in $B$
7073: uses at least one named certificate surface under \path{review_bundle/}: the
7074: manifest, certificate schema, pass-record ledger, source-interface map,
7075: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts or logs, the pinned source snapshot,
7076: or one of the case snapshots.  Therefore a submitted support surface for $B$
7077: must either contain those named files with their relative path semantics or
7078: replace them by an archive that is finite-file-list and hash equivalent.
7079: 
7080: If the exact local directory \path{review_bundle/} is present, then
7081: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness} identifies it as the
7082: current concrete local support witness and all named bundle paths are present in
7083: the local support boundary.  The file
7084: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} records the final SHA-256 digest
7085: surface for those certificate files, so the byte identity of the supplied
7086: directory is checkable without changing the role of the directory into an
7087: archive claim.  If a named bundle file is regenerated after that digest surface
7088: is written, the byte-coordinate selected by the support relation changes; by
7089: Proposition~\ref{prop:regenerated-theorem-inventory-digest-closure} and the same
7090: finite-coordinate argument, the corresponding digest row and verifier logs must
7091: be refreshed before the regenerated file can be the submitted support witness.
7092: Hence all claims in $B$ have the path-verified support surface asserted for this
7093: package exactly in the local-exact-directory-with-current-digests branch.
7094: 
7095: The archive criterion remains a finite non-current rejection test.  If a later
7096: package attempted to replace the directory by an archive, Audit
7097: record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} would require equality of
7098: the manifest identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list,
7099: per-file SHA-256 digests, and relative path semantics.  The current package does
7100: not contain the locator or archive digest table needed to enter that branch, so
7101: the theorem cannot treat an archive as an accepted present support surface.
7102: 
7103: Conversely, suppose the exact directory is not present in the current local
7104: package state.  Then at least one named bundle certificate surface is outside the
7105: local support boundary and has no selected finite replacement.  The finite certificate
7106: schema used in Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness}
7107: accepts only submitted paths, explicit historical path records, and the stated
7108: supplemental surfaces.  Hence the missing bundle surface cannot support the
7109: corresponding claim in $B$.  The public \path{newmath} repository citation is a
7110: separate pinned-source citation, so it remains available for the short
7111: architectural note but does not reconstitute the omitted bundle-backed
7112: certificate records.  This proves both admissible cases and the failure of all
7113: other cases.
7114: \end{proof}
7115: 
7116: \begin{auditrecord}[Final immutable package-state certificate]
7117: \label{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}
7118: This audit record retains the legacy cross-reference label
7119: \path{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate} for compatibility with
7120: earlier acceptance-ledger entries; its environment category is \path{auditrecord},
7121: not \path{proposition}.
7122: For the current presentation package, the final source-state record for the three
7123: finite verifier runs is the pair consisting of the source state printed in each
7124: refreshed log and the digest manifest
7125: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}; the venue/bibliography
7126: live-check run is a dated 2026-06-09 route-readiness record carrying the same
7127: digest manifest as its package-state boundary.  The selected supplemental support
7128: mode is conditional exact inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}; no DOI-bearing,
7129: institutional, or other archival replacement is claimed.  Consequently a
7130: command-result claim for any of the four logs
7131: \path{review_bundle/certificate_verification_run.log},
7132: \path{review_bundle/source_interface_verification_run.log}, or
7133: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory_freshness_2026-06-09.log}, and
7134: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log} is accepted
7135: only when read against the declared package-state boundary and the exact included
7136: bundle once the external instantiation record exists.  If either the digest
7137: manifest is absent or the exact bundle is not submitted and no archive satisfies
7138: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, the corresponding
7139: command-result and bundle-backed support claims are outside the accepted support
7140: surface of this package.
7141: \medskip
7142: \noindent\emph{Verification.} The three verifier logs and the venue/bibliography live-check log are finite
7143: files in the supplemental bundle, and their commands are the only fresh
7144: command-run surfaces listed in
7145: Table~\ref{tab:command-boundary-inventory}.  Each log records its command,
7146: environment, exit code, and log path.  After the final packaging pass the
7147: verifier logs record the source state as the displayed automath commit together
7148: with \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}; the live-check log records the
7149: dated 2026-06-09 local-date route and bibliography query tuple.  That digest manifest
7150: records the selected support mode, namely local/path-verified use of
7151: \path{review_bundle/}, and gives SHA-256 digests for the finite
7152: certificate surfaces of the package, including all four command-run logs.  Thus
7153: the byte identity of the files carrying
7154: the command-result claims is not determined by a mutable phrase such as a local
7155: working tree; it is determined by the finite commit--manifest certificate.
7156: 
7157: By Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure}, bundle-backed claims are
7158: admissible in the present package only as local exact-directory claims, and an
7159: external archive-equivalent case would require the finite locator fields of
7160: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  The final digest manifest
7161: selects the local case and states that no archive replacement is claimed; it is
7162: not itself a venue-upload receipt.  Hence the accepted support surface for this
7163: source state is precisely the local \path{review_bundle/} directory with the digest
7164: manifest serving as its byte-level final-packaging record.  If that manifest is
7165: absent, the finite source-state component attached to the logs is missing.  If the
7166: bundle is absent and no archive-equivalent replacement is supplied,
7167: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} removes the bundle-backed claims
7168: from the accepted local support surface.  These are exactly the failure cases
7169: stated in the audit record.
7170: \end{auditrecord}
